BEGIN_PGML How many dots would you expect in the next two figures in the sequence?
Dots in [`n = 5`] figure: [`a_5 = `][_]{15}{5}.
Dots in [`n = 6`] figure: [`a_6 = `][_]{21}{5}.
END_PGML
Section::End();
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML Let [`a_n`] be the number of dots in figure [`n\text{.}`] Write a recursive definition for [`a_n\text{.}`]
[@KeyboardInstructions('Use [|a(n-1)|]* for [`a_{n-1}\text{.}`]')@]**
[`a_n = `] [_]{$an}{20}; with [`a_1 = `] [_]{1}{5}.
END_PGML
Section::End();
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML Guess a closed formula for the number of dots in the [`n`]th figure.
[`a_n = `] [_]{Formula('(n*(n+1)/2)')}{20}.
END_PGML
